current code state (2026-07-11, for orientation)
------------------------------------------------

- MCP_Session.start (mcp/src/mcp_session.scala) runs Build.build +
  Headless.Resources.make over (options, session_name, session_dirs);
  NO load_structure/deps object exists anywhere yet.
- mcp_resource_read resolves image-tier theories via image_theory
  (verbatim / session-qualified / unique-base-name normalization —
  keep that lesson, see the comment block at mcp_session.scala:408)
  and loaded-tier diagnostics/entities via theory_master_dirs +
  snapshots; everything else hits the not_yet_backed_uri error that
  names this wave.
- KNOWN DEFECT this wave fixes (spec "loaded-tier membership",
  decision 2026-07-11): theory_master_dirs records only EXPLICITLY
  requested loads, but use_theories pulls in the transitive import
  closure as live document nodes — so a transitive import (including
  one an agent just added to a header on disk) answers the
  filesystem "not checked" line on /diagnostics moments after being
  checked live. tier must follow the document, not the bookkeeping.
- load_theory/check_theory take (name, master_dir) and resolve via
  resources.import_name(Sessions.DRAFT, master_dir, name): a bare
  session-qualified name with no master_dir does not find its file.

infrastructure (the D1 object, expanded)
----------------------------------------

one value computed at server startup from the SAME (options,
session_dirs) the server was given — a registered AFP shows up with
zero extra work — and kept on MCP_Session:

  structure  = Sessions.load_structure(options, dirs = session_dirs)
  deps       = Sessions.deps over the full selection (header parsing
               only; spec-verified: 134 sessions, seconds, no heaps)
  store      = Store(options)   (heap_present lookups at CALL time,
               so heaps built after startup are seen — pinned in
               plans/list_sessions T3)

derived maps, computed once:

  sessions   : name -> (chapter, description, theories)
  theory_map : theory long name -> (session, source Path)
               (from each session's known/used theories in deps; this
               is the "uri -> path resolution" the spec says the deps
               object also answers)
  base_names : base name -> List[long name]  (for the unique-base-name
               resolution rule, now over the WHOLE structure, not just
               the image — see resolution below)

resolution: ONE function replaces/extends image_theory —

  resolve_theory(name): Option[(long_name, Tier, Option[Path])]

  tier order is authoritative and checked in this order:
    image      resources.session_base.loaded_theories (existing
               image_theory logic verbatim — its normalization rules
               are load-bearing, see CHANGELOG 2026-07-10 retraction)
    loaded     the current PIDE document version's non-empty nodes
               (session.snapshot().version.nodes, matched by theory
               name) — NOT theory_master_dirs keys. this is the
               loaded-tier correction (spec decision 2026-07-11):
               use_theories loads the transitive import closure as
               document nodes, so transitive imports ARE loaded and
               must say so. skip empty nodes: purged nodes can
               linger as empty entries in the version (verify in
               A8's test). theory_master_dirs is DEMOTED to
               explicit-load bookkeeping: unload_theory eligibility
               ("was not loaded" for never-requested names) and
               master_dir recall — it no longer answers tier, and
               /diagnostics' node lookup goes through the document
               node found here rather than reconstructing a
               node_name from the recorded master_dir.
    filesystem theory_map lookup: verbatim, then unique base-name
               match. AMBIGUITY IS AN ANSWER, not a guess: two
               structure theories sharing a base name -> None from
               the base-name rule; the error message lists the
               candidates so the client can qualify.

startup cost decision: compute structure+deps EAGERLY at startup,
synchronously — seconds against the distribution, amortized over the
session lifetime, and it keeps every discovery call pure over
immutable data (no lazy-init races with the Synchronized promise
machinery). if AFP-scale dirs push this past ~10s in practice, demote
to a Future set at startup and joined on first use — decide by
measuring in step 1, pin whichever holds with the T-startup test.

implementation steps
--------------------

1. [infra] load_structure + deps + store at startup; the three derived
   maps; resolve_theory subsuming image_theory (image_theory stays as
   a thin wrapper or is inlined — its tests keep passing verbatim).
   measure startup delta; pin eager vs Future per the decision above.
2. [resources] mcp_resource_read: theory_source_uri and
   theory_commands_uri gain a filesystem-tier branch reading the file
   at theory_map's path (source = File.read; commands = the span
   question, see A4 below); /diagnostics and /entities gain the tier
   answer ("filesystem theory — not checked; load_theory to get
   semantics") for structure-known names; not_yet_backed_uri now only
   catches names outside the structure entirely — reword it to say
   "unknown theory" with a pointer at list_theories/search_sources.
   theory_diagnostics' loaded branch switches from theory_master_dirs
   + import_name reconstruction to the document node resolve_theory
   found (the loaded-tier correction) — transitive imports get the
   live snapshot read, same as explicit loads. unload_theory is
   UNCHANGED: still keyed on theory_master_dirs (explicit loads
   only), still sweeping unrequired transitive imports via
   clean_theories.
3. [load_theory] resolve session-qualified names with no master_dir
   through theory_map: pass the resolved path's directory as
   master_dir into the existing use_theories path (the wave-2
   machinery is unchanged downstream). check_theory identically.
4. [tools] land plans/list_sessions, plans/list_theories,
   plans/search_sources on top (their own steps and tests; they are
   pure functions over the maps above plus store lookups).
5. tests (below + the per-tool plans').

assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

(testing process per plans/README: [scala unit] = munit over
Fake_Backend in mcp_test/src/mcp_handler_tests.scala — but note most
cases here are pure functions over a REAL structure, no backend
needed; [bridge] = mcp_test/src/mcp_bridge_tests.scala over
MCP_Session_Suite; run isabelle mcp_test [-b] [-t PATTERN]. remember
the scala-rebuild rule: isabelle scala_build -f after edits.)

A1  D1 (restated from plans/list_sessions, implementation moved
    here): load_structure + deps over the bundled distribution
    enumerates HOL and HOL-Library with nonempty theory lists,
    chapters, descriptions; theory_map holds HOL-Library.Multiset
    with an existing source path; store answers heap_present for the
    base image.
    test [scala unit]: pure, against the real bundled distribution.
A2  startup cost: structure+deps computation stays within interactive
    startup budget (seconds) on the configured dirs.
    test [scala unit, timed loosely]: construction < generous bound;
    revisit if AFP dirs are added to the test environment.
A3  resolve_theory tier truthfulness and precedence: (a) HOL.Main ->
    image even though it also appears in the structure (image wins);
    (b) a load_theory'd fixture -> loaded, back to filesystem after
    unload_theory; (c) HOL-Library.Multiset -> filesystem + path;
    (d) unknown name -> None; (e) ambiguous base name across two
    structure sessions -> None from the base-name rule (candidates
    surfaced in the caller's error).
    test [scala unit] for (a,c,d,e) pure; [bridge] for (b), riding
    the existing wave-2 load/unload suite.
A4  /commands for filesystem theories: command spans need outer
    syntax. VERIFY BY SPIKE before step 2: scala-side
    Outer_Syntax.parse_spans with the owning session's syntax from
    deps gives usable {command, offset} spans for an unloaded .thy.
    if the per-session syntax is not cheaply reachable from deps,
    FALL BACK and pin: filesystem /commands answers the tier line
    ("filesystem theory — command map needs load_theory") and only
    the bare source uri is widened — the spec's wording ("{name}
    (and /commands) resolves ... through the path map") permits
    reading, not necessarily span-mapping, and honesty beats a
    half-right span table.
    test: [scala unit] either the spans of a fixture .thy or the
    pinned fallback message.
A5  resource widening end to end (the testing-checklist rows):
    resources/read on isabelle://theory/HOL-Library.Multiset serves
    file content WITHOUT loading it; /diagnostics on it answers the
    "not checked" tier line, not an error; a name in no session ->
    the reworded unknown-theory error.
    test [bridge]: all three against the live server.
A6  load_theory session-qualified resolution: {"name":
    "HOL-Library.Multiset"} with no master_dir resolves and starts
    checking (assert resolution + node appearance, not completion —
    deep imports are minutes; use a SHALLOW filesystem fixture
    theory in a test session for the full ok round trip).
    test [bridge]: shallow fixture full loop; resolution-only
    assertion for the deep case if kept at all.
A7  nothing regresses for image names: the wave-2 image_theory tests
    (normalization matrix: base name, session-qualified, foreign
    qualifier, ambiguous) pass unchanged through resolve_theory.
    test [scala unit]: existing cases re-pointed, plus [bridge]
    suites stay green.
A8  loaded tier follows the document (the spec's 2026-07-11
    loaded-tier decision; the testing-checklist row added with it):
    with fixture theories A imports B (both filesystem, shallow),
    load_theory A ->
    (a) resolve_theory B = loaded; list_theories reports B "loaded";
    (b) /diagnostics on B answers live (not "not checked");
    (c) unload_theory B alone -> "was not loaded" error (explicit-
        load bookkeeping untouched by the correction);
    (d) unload_theory A -> B reverts to filesystem (clean_theories
        sweeps unrequired nodes), and the empty-node caveat is
        exercised: after the sweep, resolve_theory B must NOT report
        loaded off a lingering empty version node;
    (e) the dependency-edit path: append "imports B" to a loaded
        fixture's header ON DISK, check_theory it -> B appears
        loaded, per-node report names it (use_theories recomputes
        the closure from the header, nothing cached).
    test [bridge]: one suite over the fixture pair, riding the
    wave-2 load/unload machinery; (a)'s pure precedence half also
    [scala unit] on canned node sets.

